@startuml ddc_recovery_state
!include ../dark-theme.puml
title DDC recovery state machine\nFresh helper escalation, durable identity, no healthy-row sweep

state Healthy : SliderState != Failed\n!IsReadDegraded\nbrightness target completes only after matching read-back
state Failed : SliderState == Failed\nLastDDCError set\nentry target invalidated\nnormal + immediate queues dropped\nimmutable recovery identity retained
state ReadDegraded : SliderState != Failed\nIsReadDegraded == true\nslider operable\nevery user write still attempts read-back
state PoweredOff : SliderState != Failed\nholds the app's power-off intent\n(PowerOffIntent HardOff for 0xD6=0x05, else Off)\ncurve ticks and replays refused\nstill a recovery candidate

[*] --> Healthy

Healthy --> Healthy : native read/write FAIL\nResetDDCTransport retires only this helper\nretry with a fresh process context
Healthy --> Failed : current write retries exhausted\nOR current verification exhausted\n(a reply naming another value marks the row as contradicted)\nOR Refresh re-probe exhausted\nOR known-DDC monitor disappears
Healthy --> PoweredOff : SetPowerStateAsync(off) publishes the intent\nbefore the power SET; an accepted off\nraises DDCRecoveryRequested to watch the panel

PoweredOff --> PoweredOff : targeted read fails: reads only\nHardOff + garbled reply: resend LastBusBrightness,\nwait 250 ms, read back (an acknowledgement proves nothing)
PoweredOff --> Healthy : user brightness change (setter or EnqueueUserBrightness)\nOR power-on request\nOR a reply whose power mode reads on (Refresh or recovery,\nnever while the row's own power command is still verifying):\nfresh DDC snapshot, intent lifted, current target replayed
PoweredOff --> Failed : Refresh re-probe exhausted\n(intent kept)

Failed --> Failed : DDCRecoveryRequested(id)\nworker performs immediate targeted pass
Failed --> Failed : targeted read fails\noptional last-verified write probe also fails
Failed --> ReadDegraded : targeted read fails\nwrite transport accepted\npost-write read still fails\nprobe was generic, blind, or after a checksum failure\nno read-back has contradicted an acknowledged SET\nsince this row's last confirmed write
Failed --> Healthy : targeted or post-write read succeeds\nPromoteRecovered + restore projections\npublish MonitorsRefreshed\nforce final owner target through SET + read-back

ReadDegraded --> ReadDegraded : targeted read still fails\nupdate LastDDCError only\nno periodic write probe
ReadDegraded --> Healthy : targeted read succeeds\nPromoteRecovered clears IsReadDegraded\npublish MonitorsRefreshed\nforce final owner target through SET + read-back
ReadDegraded --> Failed : active SET retries exhaust\nwrite transport is no longer usable
ReadDegraded --> Failed : a verification reply names another value\nthe acknowledged SET was not applied\nrow marked as contradicted

note bottom of Failed
  MonitorService raises DDCRecoveryRequested synchronously on demotion.
  MonitorsRefreshed also rechecks candidate state. The first worker
  pass is immediate; later passes wait 2 seconds while candidates remain.

  Candidate snapshot failure is not authoritative emptiness: the global
  recovery-needed flag remains set and the next delayed pass retries.
  Only a successful empty snapshot clears the flag and stops the worker.

  Profile-restored IsPoweredOn is not a recovery gate. A row whose
  power-off VCP was accepted in this application lifetime stays a
  candidate, probed with reads: no write probe or blind write. A HardOff
  row whose reads come back garbled gets one SET of LastBusBrightness and
  a read-back, since only its button wakes it. A reply promotes it unless
  the panel's power mode reports standby or off.

  Promotion preserves pre-failure Disabled and CurveReleased ownership;
  remaining rows resolve against the current curve/disabled-period flags.
  A curve re-engage while the row is Failed or disconnected ends a
  stashed CurveReleased first, so the row resumes curve control.

  MonitorsRefreshed subscribers reconcile ownership synchronously before
  recovery replay resolves CurveActive / CurveSleeping / CurveReleased.
  The recovery GET proves readability only. Even a matching reply receives
  one forced SET plus the normal matching read-back verification.

  A readable promotion clears stale runtime power-off suppression after an
  external wake. Background curve writes cannot clear an active gate; a
  user brightness change, through the setter or EnqueueUserBrightness,
  is explicit newer intent and clears it.
end note

note bottom of ReadDegraded
  ReadDegraded is an explicit compatibility compromise for panels
  whose DDC write transport is accepted while replies are broken.
  Transport acceptance is never persisted as applied. Read recovery
  or a normal target's matching read-back is required for proof.
  It survives only unreadable verifications. TrayDiag prints
  degraded=True for it, so eff there is intent, not panel state.

  A DP-to-HDMI converter acknowledges SETs for a dark panel, and a
  freshly booted LG answers reads before it applies SETs. Once any
  read-back contradicts an acknowledged SET, recovery sends no
  generic or blind probe and keeps the row Failed until a matching
  read-back confirms a write; the resync SET for garbled replies still
  runs but promotes only on a confirming read.
end note

note as N_HELPER
  Fresh-process escalation:
  - Failed brightness GET/SET, transport-probe SET, and power SET reset transport
  - The stable-identity helper is removed and disposed
  - The next attempt launches a new helper and dxva2 process context
  - Helper-side identity resolution uses lightweight Win32 + EDID only
  - A positive operation timeout is mandatory in the tray process
end note

note as N_ISOLATION
  Recovery isolation and responsiveness:
  - Candidate monitors run in parallel; each monitor remains serialized
  - Healthy rows receive no collateral recovery reads unless they hold a power-off intent
  - Failed rows keep DeviceID / instance / serial / adapter identity
  - Native hangs/timeouts kill only the affected helper process
  - Recovery has no terminal attempt count while a candidate remains
  - Promotion adds one verified replay, never a periodic SET loop
end note

note as N_REMAINING
  Remaining boundaries:
  - Each candidate still performs its own complete parent enumeration
  - Runtime power-off intent limits probing to reads, plus one LastBusBrightness SET after a hard off
  - ReadDegraded cannot prove application until replies recover
  - Native failure categories remain flattened into error strings
  - Endless recovery is limited to previously successful DDC rows
  - Per-op timeout is bounded; whole-sequence deadline is not
end note

@enduml
